      "id": "9d9fb4eb-4f0f-4a6f-bc72-0b1a8cdc407b",
      "text": "Project Madar documents `JournalPolicy` and `BalancedJournal` as an implemented pure-contract candidate for FIN-01/02 validation. `JournalPolicy` explicitly declares currency, scale, maximum line and side amounts, line count, and zero-line permission; `BalancedJournal.validate` enforces identifier validity, line units, nonnegative bounded amounts, side totals, and exact debit/credit equality, returning immutable lines and totals with structural failure codes without rejected payloads. The journal contract also requires balanced immutable lines and inverse journals under an explicit single-currency policy, while durable identity uniqueness, account mapping, and posting atomicity remain caller responsibilities. The implementation has no float, storage, clock, logging, or network dependencies. Independent pure-contract review is complete, but consumer adoption, restaurant account mapping, durable posting, and migration remain pending.",
